              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lisa Bunting"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I did it slightly different according to what I had but it was still so good. I used dried minced garlic, I did not have MSG and used a small amount of sea salt in its place. Also low sodium soy sauce. The mirin is what makes it imo. I fried it up on the stove instead of doing it in the broiler.. fantastic flavor and my 4 and 6 year old loved it too with a bit of jasmine rice."
